# AQL and inspection templates (TECH 4, FI 1 AQL). Sampling plans are entered by the organization; no published sampling table is reproduced.

block insp_header
section insp_lot | Lot and inspection | 3
f insp_part_number | Part number | text | *
f insp_part_revision | Revision | text
f insp_lot | Lot or batch | text | *
f insp_lot_size | Lot size | integer | * min=1
f insp_plan | Inspection plan | record
f insp_plan_revision | Plan revision | text
f insp_inspector | Inspector | user | *
f insp_date | Inspection date | date | *
f insp_location | Location | text
end

block insp_sampling
section sampling | Sampling | 3 | Enter the sample size and the accept and reject numbers from the organization's approved sampling plan for this lot size and inspection level.
f smp_plan_type | Sampling plan | choice | * [Single sampling; Double sampling; Zero acceptance; 100 percent; Skip lot]
f smp_level | Inspection level | choice | [Reduced; Normal; Tightened]
f smp_aql | AQL | number | dec=3 min=0
f smp_size | Sample size | integer | * min=1
f smp_accept | Accept number | integer | * min=0
f smp_reject | Reject number | integer | * min=1
f smp_defectives | Defectives found | calc | {SUM(insp_chars.ic_rejected)}
f smp_decision | Sampling decision | calc | {IF(smp_defectives <= smp_accept, "ACCEPT", IF(smp_defectives >= smp_reject, "REJECT", "SECOND SAMPLE"))}
f smp_percent | Percent defective in sample | calc | {IF(smp_size > 0, smp_defectives / smp_size * 100, 0)} dec=2 unit=%
check smp_reject | greaterThan | smp_accept | The reject number must be greater than the accept number.
check smp_size | lessOrEqual | insp_lot_size | The sample size cannot exceed the lot size.
rule smp_decision | equals | REJECT | #FDE7E9 | bold
rule smp_decision | equals | ACCEPT | #E6F4EA | bold
rule smp_decision | equals | SECOND SAMPLE | #FFF4D6 | bold
end

block insp_characteristics
section insp_char_section | Characteristic results | 1
table insp_chars | Characteristics | 1
groups Characteristic:3; Specification:3; Results:4
c ic_char | Characteristic | text | *
c ic_class | Class | choice | [Critical; Major; Minor]
c ic_method | Method or gauge | text
c ic_nominal | Nominal | number | dec=4
c ic_lsl | Lower limit | number | dec=4
c ic_usl | Upper limit | number | dec=4
c ic_checked | Checked | integer | * min=0
c ic_rejected | Rejected | integer | * min=0
c ic_equipment | Equipment | equipment
c ic_result | Result | calc | {IF(ic_rejected = 0, "PASS", "FAIL")}
rule insp_chars.ic_result | equals | FAIL | #FDE7E9 | bold
rule insp_chars.ic_class | equals | Critical | #FFF4D6 | bold
total ic_checked | sum | Checked
total ic_rejected | sum | Rejected
end

block insp_disposition
section lot_disposition | Lot disposition | 2
f lot_decision | Lot decision | choice | * [Accepted; Rejected; Accepted with deviation; Sort 100 percent; Hold pending review]
f lot_ncr | Nonconformance | record | reqwhen=lot_decision=Rejected
f lot_deviation | Deviation reference | text | when=lot_decision=Accepted_with_deviation
f lot_stock_status | Stock status set to | choice | [Released; Quarantined; Returned; Scrapped]
f lot_notes | Notes | longtext
rule lot_decision | equals | Rejected | #FDE7E9 | bold
end

block insp_signatures
sign insp_performed | Inspected by | performed | I performed this inspection and recorded the results as found.
sign insp_verified | Verified by | verified | I verified the results and the lot decision. | inspection.edit
sign insp_approved | Approved by | approved | I approve the disposition of this lot. | inspection.approve | optional
end

template receiving-inspection | Receiving Inspection | INSPECTION
packs manufacturing
tags inspection, receiving, incoming, AQL
purpose Inspect purchased material and parts on receipt against the purchase order, the specification and the inspection plan, and decide whether the lot is released to stock.
scope Purchased material, parts and services that the inspection plan requires to be inspected on receipt.
instructions Check the paperwork first, then sample the lot as the plan requires. Record each characteristic. A rejected lot is quarantined and a supplier nonconformance is raised.
workflow Received, inspected, verified, released or quarantined.
retention Keep for the life of the product plus the retention period set by the organization.
use insp_header
section receipt | Receipt | 3
f rcv_supplier | Supplier | supplier | *
f rcv_po | Purchase order | text | *
f rcv_packing_slip | Packing slip or delivery note | text
f rcv_received_on | Received on | date | *
f rcv_qty_received | Quantity received | integer | * min=0
f rcv_qty_ordered | Quantity ordered | integer | min=0
f rcv_qty_check | Quantity matches the order | calc | {IF(rcv_qty_received = rcv_qty_ordered, "Yes", "No")}
section documents_check | Documents | 1
table doc_checks | Documents received | 0
rows Certificate of conformance; Material certificate; Test report; First article report; Packing slip; Customs or dangerous goods paperwork
c dc_required | Required | boolean
c dc_received | Received | boolean
c dc_acceptable | Acceptable | passfail
c dc_reference | Reference | text
rule doc_checks.dc_acceptable | equals | FAIL | #FDE7E9 | bold
use insp_sampling, insp_characteristics, insp_disposition, insp_signatures
end

template in-process-inspection | In-Process Inspection | INSPECTION
packs manufacturing
tags inspection, in-process, patrol
purpose Check product at defined operations during production so that nonconforming work is stopped before it moves on.
scope Operations where the control plan specifies an in-process check.
instructions Inspect at the frequency the control plan states. When a check fails, stop, contain the work since the last good check and follow the reaction plan.
workflow Checked at frequency, failures contained, verified.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization.
use insp_header
section operation | Operation | 3
f ip_operation | Operation | text | *
f ip_machine | Machine or work centre | text
f ip_shift | Shift | choice | [Day; Afternoon; Night]
f ip_frequency | Frequency | text
f ip_work_order | Work order | text
use insp_characteristics
section reaction | Reaction | 2
f ip_failures | Characteristics failed | calc | {COUNTIF(insp_chars.ic_result, "FAIL")}
f ip_reaction | Reaction plan followed | longtext | reqwhen=ip_reaction_needed=true
f ip_reaction_needed | Reaction needed | boolean
f ip_contained_from | Contained back to | datetime | when=ip_reaction_needed=true
use insp_signatures
end

template final-inspection | Final Inspection | INSPECTION
packs manufacturing
tags inspection, final, release
purpose Confirm that finished product meets every requirement before it is released for shipment, including the evidence that all planned inspections were completed.
scope Finished product before release.
instructions Confirm the earlier inspections are complete. Sample the finished lot as the plan requires and record the results. Release only when every check passes.
workflow Inspected, verified, released or held.
retention Keep for the life of the product plus the retention period set by the organization.
use insp_header
section prior_checks | Prior checks | 1
table prior_rows | Earlier inspections complete | 0
rows Receiving inspection; In-process inspection; Functional test; Packaging and labelling; Traveller or route card complete
c pr_complete | Complete | choice | * [Yes; No; Not applicable]
c pr_reference | Reference | text
rule prior_rows.pr_complete | equals | No | #FDE7E9 | bold
use insp_sampling, insp_characteristics, insp_disposition, insp_signatures
end

template first-piece-inspection | First-Piece Inspection | INSPECTION
packs manufacturing
tags inspection, first piece, set-up approval
purpose Approve the first part produced after a set-up, tool change, material change or long stoppage before the run continues.
scope Every set-up and change the control plan names.
instructions Run the first piece and inspect every characteristic in the plan. The run may continue only after the first piece is approved. Retain the piece where the plan requires.
workflow Set-up, first piece inspected, approved, run released.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization.
use insp_header
section setup | Set-up | 3
f fp_trigger | Reason | choice | * [New set-up; Tool change; Material change; Operator change; Stoppage over limit; Repair; Programme change]
f fp_machine | Machine | text | *
f fp_tool | Tool or fixture | text
f fp_program | Programme and revision | text
f fp_setter | Set up by | user
use insp_characteristics
section fp_outcome | Outcome | 2
f fp_result | First piece result | calc | {IF(COUNTIF(insp_chars.ic_result, "FAIL") = 0, "APPROVED", "REJECTED")}
f fp_retained | First piece retained | boolean
f fp_released_at | Run released at | datetime
rule fp_result | equals | REJECTED | #FDE7E9 | bold
use insp_signatures
end

template dock-audit | Dock Audit | INSPECTION
packs manufacturing
tags inspection, dock audit, outgoing
purpose Audit packed product at the shipping dock from the customer's point of view: right part, right quantity, right labels, right packaging and right documents.
scope Shipments selected by the dock audit plan.
instructions Select the shipments at the frequency set by the plan. Open the packaging, check each item and record the result. Failures stop the shipment.
workflow Selected, audited, shipped or held.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization.
section dock | Shipment | 3
f da_shipment | Shipment or order | text | *
f da_customer_ship | Ship-to | text
f da_containers | Containers audited | integer | min=1
f da_auditor | Auditor | user | *
f da_date | Date | date | *
section dock_checks | Checks | 1
table dock_rows | Checks | 0
rows Correct part number; Correct revision; Correct quantity per container; Label content and placement; Barcode readable; Packaging as specified; Product condition; No foreign material; Shipping documents; Certificate of conformance
c dk_result | Result | passfail
c dk_note | Note | text
rule dock_rows.dk_result | equals | FAIL | #FDE7E9 | bold
section dock_outcome | Outcome | 2
f dk_failures | Checks failed | calc | {COUNTIF(dock_rows.dk_result, "FAIL")}
f dk_decision | Decision | calc | {IF(dk_failures = 0, "SHIP", "HOLD")}
rule dk_decision | equals | HOLD | #FDE7E9 | bold
use insp_signatures
end

template packaging-inspection | Packaging Inspection | INSPECTION
packs manufacturing
tags inspection, packaging, labelling
purpose Verify that packaging and labelling meet the packaging specification before product is packed or shipped.
scope Packaging lines and packed product as the plan requires.
instructions Check the packaging specification revision, the materials and each label. Record the measurement where the specification sets a limit.
workflow Inspected, verified, released.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization.
use insp_header
section pkg_spec | Specification | 3
f pkg_spec | Packaging specification | text | *
f pkg_spec_rev | Revision | text
f pkg_type | Packaging type | choice | [Returnable; Expendable; Customer supplied]
section pkg_checks | Checks | 1
table pkg_rows | Checks | 0
rows Container type; Dunnage and separators; Quantity per layer; Layers per container; Container weight; Moisture or corrosion protection; Seal or tamper evidence; Part label; Container label; Master label
c pk_requirement | Requirement | text
c pk_actual | Actual | text
c pk_result | Result | passfail
rule pkg_rows.pk_result | equals | FAIL | #FDE7E9 | bold
f pkg_failures | Checks failed | calc | {COUNTIF(pkg_rows.pk_result, "FAIL")}
use insp_disposition, insp_signatures
end

template sample-inspection | Sample Inspection | INSPECTION
packs manufacturing
tags inspection, sampling, AQL, sampling inspection
purpose Inspect a sample drawn from a lot to the organization's approved sampling plan and decide the lot from the number of defectives found.
scope Lots inspected by sampling rather than 100 percent.
instructions Draw the sample at random across the lot. Enter the sample size and accept and reject numbers from the approved plan. The decision is calculated from the defectives found.
workflow Sampled, inspected, decided, verified.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization.
use insp_header, insp_sampling, insp_characteristics, insp_disposition, insp_signatures
end

template lot-acceptance-inspection | Lot Acceptance Inspection | INSPECTION
packs manufacturing
tags inspection, lot acceptance, lot inspection, AQL
purpose Decide whether a lot is accepted, rejected or sorted, on the basis of a sample inspection and the lot's documentation, and record the decision with its authority.
scope Lots presented for acceptance: purchased, produced or returned.
instructions Inspect the sample as the plan requires. Record any defect by class. The lot decision follows the sampling decision unless an authorized person records a deviation.
workflow Sampled, inspected, decided, approved.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization.
use insp_header, insp_sampling, insp_characteristics
section defects_by_class | Defects by class | 3
f lai_critical | Critical defects | integer | min=0
f lai_major | Major defects | integer | min=0
f lai_minor | Minor defects | integer | min=0
f lai_critical_reject | Critical defect found | calc | {IF(lai_critical > 0, "Yes", "No")}
rule lai_critical_reject | equals | Yes | #FDE7E9 | bold
use insp_disposition, insp_signatures
end

template skip-lot-inspection | Skip-Lot Inspection | INSPECTION
packs manufacturing
tags inspection, skip lot
purpose Record a lot received under skip-lot status: whether the lot was selected for inspection or skipped, and the result when inspected.
scope Part and supplier combinations qualified for skip-lot inspection.
instructions Confirm the skip-lot status is current. Lots selected by the skip frequency are inspected to the sampling plan; skipped lots are released on documentation review. A rejected lot returns the part to normal inspection.
workflow Received, selected or skipped, inspected where selected, released.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization.
use insp_header
section skip_status | Skip-lot status | 3
f sl_review | Qualifying skip-lot review | record
f sl_frequency | Skip frequency (inspect 1 in N lots) | integer | * min=1
f sl_lot_sequence | Lot sequence number since qualification | integer | * min=1
f sl_selected | Lot selected for inspection | calc | {IF(MOD(sl_lot_sequence, sl_frequency) = 0, "Yes", "No")}
f sl_docs_ok | Documentation acceptable | passfail | *
use insp_sampling, insp_characteristics, insp_disposition, insp_signatures
end

template skip-lot-review | Skip-Lot Review | INSPECTION
packs manufacturing
tags inspection, skip lot, qualification
purpose Decide whether a part and supplier combination qualifies for, stays on, or leaves skip-lot inspection, from its recent lot history.
scope Part and supplier combinations considered for reduced inspection.
instructions Enter the recent lot history. The organization sets the number of consecutive accepted lots and the period needed to qualify. Any rejection, supplier change or process change removes the status.
workflow History reviewed, decision approved, reviewed at the set interval.
retention Keep while the status applies plus the retention period set by the organization.
section skip_subject | Subject | 3
f slr_supplier | Supplier | supplier | *
f slr_part | Part | part | *
f slr_required_lots | Consecutive accepted lots required | integer | * min=1
f slr_period | Review period | choice | [3 months; 6 months; 12 months]
section skip_history | Lot history | 1
table slr_lots | Recent lots | 1
c slr_lot | Lot | text | *
c slr_date | Received | date
c slr_result | Result | choice | * [Accepted; Rejected]
c slr_record | Inspection record | record
rule slr_lots.slr_result | equals | Rejected | #FDE7E9 | bold
section skip_decision | Decision | 2
f slr_accepted | Lots accepted | calc | {COUNTIF(slr_lots.slr_result, "Accepted")}
f slr_rejected | Lots rejected | calc | {COUNTIF(slr_lots.slr_result, "Rejected")}
f slr_qualifies | Meets the qualification rule | calc | {IF(AND(slr_rejected = 0, slr_accepted >= slr_required_lots), "Yes", "No")}
f slr_decision | Decision | choice | * [Qualify for skip lot; Remain on skip lot; Return to normal inspection]
f slr_next_review | Next review | date
end

template inspection-plan-template | Inspection Plan | INSPECTION
packs manufacturing
tags inspection plan, characteristics, sampling
purpose Define what is inspected for a part at each inspection point: characteristics, methods, equipment, sample size, frequency and reaction.
scope Parts that need receiving, in-process or final inspection.
instructions List every characteristic with its specification and method. Set the sample size and frequency from the organization's sampling rules. Reference the control plan where one exists.
workflow Drafted, reviewed, approved, revised on change.
retention Keep for the life of the part plus the retention period set by the organization.
landscape
section plan_subject | Subject | 3
f ipl_part_number | Part number | text | *
f ipl_revision | Part revision | text | *
f ipl_type | Inspection type | choice | * [Receiving; In-process; Final; First piece; Audit]
f ipl_control_plan | Control plan | record
f ipl_aql | Default AQL | number | dec=3 min=0
section plan_chars | Characteristics | 1
table ipl_rows | Characteristics | 1
groups Characteristic:3; Specification:3; Method:4
c pl_char | Characteristic | text | *
c pl_class | Class | choice | * [Critical; Major; Minor]
c pl_balloon | Balloon | text
c pl_nominal | Nominal | number | dec=4
c pl_lsl | Lower limit | number | dec=4
c pl_usl | Upper limit | number | dec=4
c pl_method | Method | text | *
c pl_equipment | Equipment | equipment
c pl_sample | Sample size | text | *
c pl_frequency | Frequency | text | *
rule ipl_rows.pl_class | equals | Critical | #FFF4D6 | bold
section plan_reaction | Reaction | 1
f ipl_reaction | Reaction plan | longtext | *
use approval_trio
end

template characteristic-results | Characteristic Results | INSPECTION
packs manufacturing
tags inspection, results, variables
purpose Record variable measurements for characteristics, with summary statistics calculated live for each characteristic.
scope Inspections that record measured values.
instructions Enter the limits and up to ten measured values for each characteristic. Mean, range, standard deviation and the result are calculated.
workflow Measured, reviewed, verified.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization.
landscape
use insp_header
section var_results | Measurements | 1
table var_rows | Characteristics | 1
groups Characteristic:3; Values:5; Statistics:4
c vr_char | Characteristic | text | *
c vr_lsl | Lower limit | number | dec=4
c vr_usl | Upper limit | number | dec=4
c vr_v1 | Value 1 | number | dec=4
c vr_v2 | Value 2 | number | dec=4
c vr_v3 | Value 3 | number | dec=4
c vr_v4 | Value 4 | number | dec=4
c vr_v5 | Value 5 | number | dec=4
c vr_mean | Mean | calc | {AVERAGE(vr_v1, vr_v2, vr_v3, vr_v4, vr_v5)} dec=4
c vr_range | Range | calc | {MAX(vr_v1, vr_v2, vr_v3, vr_v4, vr_v5) - MIN(vr_v1, vr_v2, vr_v3, vr_v4, vr_v5)} dec=4
c vr_sd | Std dev | calc | {STDEV(vr_v1, vr_v2, vr_v3, vr_v4, vr_v5)} dec=5
c vr_result | Result | calc | {IF(AND(OR(ISBLANK(vr_lsl), MIN(vr_v1, vr_v2, vr_v3, vr_v4, vr_v5) >= vr_lsl), OR(ISBLANK(vr_usl), MAX(vr_v1, vr_v2, vr_v3, vr_v4, vr_v5) <= vr_usl)), "PASS", "FAIL")}
rule var_rows.vr_result | equals | FAIL | #FDE7E9 | bold
f vr_failed | Characteristics failed | calc | {COUNTIF(var_rows.vr_result, "FAIL")}
use insp_signatures
end

template defect-summary | Defect Summary | INSPECTION
packs manufacturing
tags inspection, defects, Pareto
purpose Summarize the defects found over a period by type, with counts, share and cumulative share for Pareto analysis.
scope Any inspection point or product over a reporting period.
instructions Enter each defect type with its count. Share and cumulative share are calculated; sort by count, highest first, before review.
workflow Compiled, reviewed, actions assigned.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization.
section summary_scope | Scope | 3
f ds_from | Period from | date | *
f ds_to | Period to | date | *
f ds_area | Inspection point or area | text | *
f ds_inspected | Units inspected | integer | * min=0
check ds_to | greaterOrEqual | ds_from | The period end cannot be before its start.
section defects | Defects | 1
table defect_rows | Defect types | 1
c df_type | Defect type | text | *
c df_code | Code | text
c df_count | Count | integer | * min=0
c df_action | Action | text
total df_count | sum | Total defects
running df_count
f df_total | Total defects | calc | {SUM(defect_rows.df_count)}
f df_top_share | Share of the largest defect type | calc | {IF(df_total > 0, MAX(defect_rows.df_count) / df_total * 100, 0)} dec=1 unit=%
f df_ppm | Defects per million units | calc | {IF(ds_inspected > 0, df_total / ds_inspected * 1000000, 0)} dec=0
use approval_trio
end

template lot-disposition | Lot Disposition | INSPECTION
packs manufacturing
tags inspection, lot disposition, hold, release
purpose Record the authorized disposition of a lot that is held: the reason, the decision, the quantities in each outcome and the authority.
scope Lots held by inspection, by a nonconformance, or by a customer or supplier notice.
instructions State why the lot is held. The disposition is decided by an authorized person; quantities in each outcome must add up to the lot quantity.
workflow Held, dispositioned, approved, executed, verified.
retention Keep for the life of the product plus the retention period set by the organization.
use insp_header
section hold | Hold | 2
f ld_reason | Reason for hold | longtext | *
f ld_source | Raised by | choice | * [Inspection; Nonconformance; Customer notice; Supplier notice; Audit; Other]
f ld_source_record | Source record | record
section ld_outcomes | Outcomes | 1
table ld_rows | Disposition quantities | 1
c ld_outcome | Outcome | choice | * [Release; Rework; Sort; Return to supplier; Scrap; Use with deviation]
c ld_qty | Quantity | integer | * min=0
c ld_reference | Reference | text
total ld_qty | sum | Total
f ld_total | Quantity dispositioned | calc | {SUM(ld_rows.ld_qty)}
f ld_balance | Balance against lot size | calc | {insp_lot_size - ld_total}
rule ld_balance | notEquals | 0 | #FFF4D6 | bold
use insp_signatures
end
